---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import JobStories from './JobStories.astro';
import type { Service } from '../../data/site';
import { site } from '../../data/site';
import { loads, minimum, pricing, faqById } from '../../lib/site';
import { subservices, subPath } from '../../data/subservices';
import { jobsForService } from '../../lib/jobs';
import { jobImage, projectFor, fitWidths, PHOTO_QUALITY } from '../../lib/images';
import StCharlesCounty from './StCharlesCounty.astro';

interface Props { service: Service }
const { service: s } = Astro.props;
const quarter = loads.find((l) => l.id === 'quarter')!;
const half = loads.find((l) => l.id === 'half')!;
const three = loads.find((l) => l.id === 'three-quarter')!;
const full = loads.find((l) => l.id === 'full')!;
const shedFit = three.fits.find((f) => /shed/i.test(f));
const deckFit = full.fits.find((f) => /deck/i.test(f));
const recycling = faqById('recycling');
const jobs = jobsForService(s.slug === 'construction-debris-removal' ? 'construction-debris-removal' : s.slug);
const demoCards = [
  { sub: 'interior-demolition', file: 'demolition/ferguson-room-demo.jpg', text: 'Walls, drywall, flooring, ceilings and fixtures. One recorded room opening is in Ferguson.' },
  { sub: 'bathroom-demolition', file: 'demolition/webster-groves-bathroom-gutted.jpg', text: 'Tubs, showers, vanities, tile and subfloor. Four bathrooms, in Webster Groves, Manchester, Ladue and St. Charles.' },
  { sub: 'kitchen-demolition', file: 'demolition/brentwood-kitchen-countertop-backsplash-demo.jpg', text: 'Cabinets, counters, backsplash, flooring and appliances. Brentwood was tops and backsplash only, with the cabinets protected.' },
  { sub: 'commercial-interior-demolition', file: 'crew/truck.webp', text: 'Offices, shops and other commercial interiors. We don’t have a commercial job photo on the site yet. The truck is ours. The room photos are houses.' },
].map((c) => {
  const sub = subservices.find((x) => x.slug === c.sub)!;
  const photo = projectFor(c.file);
  return { ...c, sub, photo };
});
---
{s.slug === 'junk-removal' && (
  <>
    <section class="section-tight" aria-labelledby="haul-h">
      <div class="shell depth">
        <h2 id="haul-h" class="display-md">What we haul</h2>
        <p>You point. We carry it from the basement, the attic, a third floor or the backyard, load the truck and take it. The groups below are the ones on the junk removal list.</p>
        <ul class="depth__list">
          {s.scope.map((item) => (
            <li>
              <h3 class="title">{item.title}</h3>
              <p class="muted">
                {item.body}
                {item.title === 'Hot tub removal' && <> The cut-down and haul are demolition. See <a class="link-u accent" href="/services/demolition/#hot-tub-removal">hot tub removal</a>.</>}
                {item.title === 'Shed removal' && <> Taking the shed down is demolition. See <a class="link-u accent" href="/services/demolition/#shed-demolition">shed demolition</a>.</>}
              </p>
            </li>
          ))}
        </ul>
        <p>Furniture, appliances and mattresses are on that list. We don't have separate pages for them yet. Hot tubs, sheds, decks and mattresses are waiting on job photos too. Ask for them on the booking form.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="section-tight" aria-labelledby="nope-h">
      <div class="shell depth">
        <h2 id="nope-h" class="display-md">What we can't take</h2>
        <p>Tires, batteries, liquid paint, and hazardous materials: chemicals, solvents, fuel, asbestos and medical waste. If you aren't sure, ask before you book. We don't abate asbestos. Testing, when a demolition job needs it, is handled by an inspector.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="section-tight" aria-labelledby="works-h">
      <div class="shell depth">
        <h2 id="works-h" class="display-md">How a junk pickup works</h2>
        <p>Book online. Pick the load, add the address and a few photos, and choose an open arrival window. We confirm the price before anything is loaded. You don't have to be home. Make sure we can reach the pile and say where it is in the access notes.</p>
        <p>Same-day is available when the schedule has an open window at least 2 hours out. If there's one today, you'll see it while you book. Or call {site.phone}.</p>
        <p>A quarter load starts at {quarter.priceLine.amount} ({quarter.yards} cubic yards). A half starts at {half.priceLine.amount}. Three quarters starts at {three.priceLine.amount}. A full {pricing.maxCubicYards}-yard truck starts at {full.priceLine.amount}. The minimum pickup is {minimum?.priceLine.amount}. Freon items are $25 each. <a class="link-u accent" href="/pricing/">Full price breakdown</a>.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="section-tight" aria-labelledby="jobs-h">
      <div class="shell depth">
        <h2 id="jobs-h" class="display-md">Recent junk removal jobs</h2>
        <p>These are recorded jobs. The city link is there when that place has its own page.</p>
        <JobStories jobs={jobs} />
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="section-tight" aria-labelledby="where-h">
      <div class="shell depth">
        <h2 id="where-h" class="display-md">Where does it all go?</h2>
        {recycling && <p>{recycling.a}</p>}
      </div>
    </section>
  </>
)}

{s.slug === 'cleanouts' && (
  <>
    <section class="section-tight" aria-labelledby="estate-h">
      <div class="shell depth">
        <h2 id="estate-h" class="display-md">Estate cleanouts</h2>
        <p>{s.notes.find((n) => n.title.startsWith('Estates'))?.text} We set aside what the family keeps and take the rest. The space we cleared gets swept before we leave.</p>
        <p>A cleanout is still priced by the load. A quarter starts at {quarter.priceLine.amount}, a half starts at {half.priceLine.amount}, three quarters starts at {three.priceLine.amount}, and a full truck starts at {full.priceLine.amount}. If the house takes a second load, that load is priced the same way. <a class="link-u accent" href="/pricing/">See the load table</a>.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="section-tight" aria-labelledby="spaces-h">
      <div class="shell depth">
        <h2 id="spaces-h" class="display-md">Garages, basements and move-outs</h2>
        <ul class="depth__list">
          {s.scope.map((item) => <li><h3 class="title">{item.title}</h3><p class="muted">{item.body}</p></li>)}
        </ul>
        <p>Move-out and rental cleanouts are carrying jobs. If a wall, a kitchen or a bath has to come apart first, that's <a class="link-u accent" href="/services/demolition/">demolition</a>, and the debris can leave with the same crew.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="section-tight" aria-labelledby="cjobs-h">
      <div class="shell depth">
        <h2 id="cjobs-h" class="display-md">Recent cleanout jobs</h2>
        <JobStories jobs={jobs} />
      </div>
    </section>
  </>
)}

{s.slug === 'demolition' && (
  <>
    <section class="section-tight" aria-labelledby="rooms-h">
      <div class="shell">
        <div class="head">
          <h2 id="rooms-h" class="display-md">Interior, kitchen and bathroom demolition</h2>
          <p class="lead">Each room has its own page, with the job photos. This page is the overview. Commercial interiors are included.</p>
        </div>
        <ul class="cards">
          {demoCards.map((c) => (
            <li>
              <a class="card" href={subPath(c.sub)}>
                <div class="media card__photo">
                  <Image src={jobImage(c.photo.file)} alt={c.sub.slug === 'commercial-interior-demolition' ? 'Company dump truck, not a commercial job photo' : c.photo.alt} widths={fitWidths(jobImage(c.photo.file), [480, 800])} quality={PHOTO_QUALITY} sizes="(min-width: 900px) 280px, 100vw" loading="lazy" />
                </div>
                <h3 class="title">{c.sub.name}</h3>
                <p class="muted">{c.text}</p>
              </a>
            </li>
          ))}
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section-tight" aria-labelledby="structures-h">
      <div class="shell depth">
        <h2 id="structures-h" class="display-md">Garages and houses</h2>
        <!-- TODO(seo): need photos and city/date for a whole garage demolition and a whole house demolition -->
        <p>{s.scope.find((i) => i.title === 'Garage demolition')?.body} {s.scope.find((i) => i.title === 'House demolition')?.body}</p>
        <p>There isn't a garage or house job on the site yet, so this section doesn't show a photo or a city. Send pictures of the building and we'll quote the labor. The debris is hauled by the load, same as any other demo.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section-tight" aria-labelledby="concrete-h">
      <div class="shell depth">
        <h2 id="concrete-h" class="display-md">Concrete patios and driveways</h2>
        <!-- TODO(seo): need a concrete patio or driveway breakout photo with city and date -->
        <p>{s.scope.find((i) => i.title === 'Concrete breakout')?.body} Breaking the slab is labor, quoted from photos. Hauling the pieces is the load price, and heavy material adds about $75 per quarter load.</p>
        <p>If the concrete is already broken and piled up, <a class="link-u accent" href="/services/construction-debris-removal/">construction debris removal</a> is the haul.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section-tight" aria-labelledby="outdoor-h">
      <div class="shell depth">
        <h2 id="outdoor-h" class="display-md">Outdoor demolition: sheds, decks and hot tubs</h2>
        <p>These don't have their own pages. No shed, deck or hot tub job photo is on file yet. The load examples below are typical, not promises.</p>
        <h3 id="shed-demolition" class="title">Shed demolition</h3>
        <p>{s.scope.find((i) => i.title === 'Shed demolition')?.body} {shedFit ? `"${shedFit}" is listed under a three-quarter load, ${three.priceLine.label}.` : ''} {pricing.examplesNote}</p>
        <h3 id="deck-removal" class="title">Deck removal</h3>
        <p>{s.scope.find((i) => i.title === 'Deck demolition')?.body} {deckFit ? `"${deckFit}" is listed under a full load, ${full.priceLine.label}.` : ''} {pricing.examplesNote}</p>
        <h3 id="hot-tub-removal" class="title">Hot tub removal</h3>
        <p>{s.scope.find((i) => i.title === 'Hot tub removal')?.body} Labor for the cut-down is quoted per job. The haul is by the load. There isn't a hot tub line in the load examples, so we won't invent one.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section-tight" aria-labelledby="prep-h">
      <div class="shell depth">
        <h2 id="prep-h" class="display-md">Before we start: permits, utilities and what stays</h2>
        {s.notes.map((n) => <p><strong>{n.title}.</strong> {n.text}</p>)}
        <p>We can't take asbestos. Testing is handled by an inspector before demolition. We don't do abatement. Suspect material has to be cleared before we start that part of the job.</p>
        <p>Hauling starts at {quarter.priceLine.amount} for a quarter load, {half.priceLine.amount} for a half, {three.priceLine.amount} for three quarters, and {full.priceLine.amount} for the full {pricing.maxCubicYards}-yard truck. <a class="link-u accent" href="/pricing/">Full price breakdown</a>.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section-tight" aria-labelledby="djobs-h">
      <div class="shell depth">
        <h2 id="djobs-h" class="display-md">Recent demolition jobs</h2>
        <JobStories jobs={jobs} />
      </div>
    </section>
  </>
)}

{s.slug === 'construction-debris-removal' && (
  <>
    <section class="section-tight" aria-labelledby="take-h">
      <div class="shell depth">
        <h2 id="take-h" class="display-md">What construction debris we take</h2>
        <ul class="depth__list">
          {s.scope.map((item) => <li><h3 class="title">{item.title}</h3><p class="muted">{item.body}</p></li>)}
        </ul>
        <p>{s.notes.find((n) => n.title === 'Heavy stuff')?.text} Concrete, brick, dirt and shingles add about $75 per quarter load. A quarter load of ordinary debris starts at {quarter.priceLine.amount}. A full truck starts at {full.priceLine.amount}.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="section-tight" aria-labelledby="break-h">
      <div class="shell depth">
        <h2 id="break-h" class="display-md">Already broken, or still a patio?</h2>
        <p>This page is the haul. If the concrete, the deck or the kitchen is still in place, it has to be torn out first. We break out patios and driveways. That labor is quoted per job on the <a class="link-u accent" href="/services/demolition/#concrete-h">demolition page</a>. Room tear-outs are <a class="link-u accent" href="/services/demolition/interior-demolition/">interior</a>, <a class="link-u accent" href="/services/demolition/kitchen-demolition/">kitchen</a> and <a class="link-u accent" href="/services/demolition/bathroom-demolition/">bathroom</a> demolition.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="section-tight" aria-labelledby="crews-h">
      <div class="shell depth">
        <h2 id="crews-h" class="display-md">For contractors: recurring job-site pickups</h2>
        <p>{s.notes.find((n) => n.title === 'Contractors')?.text} Homeowners mid-remodel use the same truck between phases. We show up, load the pile and take it. Mention concrete, brick, dirt or shingles when you book so the truck comes set up for the weight. The price is confirmed before the first piece goes on. The three debris jobs on file are in Ballwin, Hazelwood and Affton. Affton sits on the <a class="link-u accent" href="/service-areas/south-county/#affton">South County page</a>.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="section-tight" aria-labelledby="dj-h">
      <div class="shell depth">
        <h2 id="dj-h" class="display-md">Recent debris jobs</h2>
        <JobStories jobs={jobs} />
      </div>
    </section>
  </>
)}

<StCharlesCounty />

<style>
  .depth { display: grid; gap: 16px; }
  .depth p, .depth li p { max-width: 68ch; }
  .depth__list { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; display: grid; gap: 14px; }
  .depth__list li { display: grid; gap: 4px; }
  .cards { list-style: none; margin: 28px 0 0; padding: 0; display: grid; gap: 16px; }
  @media (min-width: 800px) { .cards { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; } }
  .card { display: grid; gap: 10px; height: 100%; padding: 12px; border-radius: var(--radius-lg); background: var(--color-card); box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px var(--color-line); }
  .card__photo { aspect-ratio: 4 / 3; }
  .card:hover { background: var(--color-card-2); }
</style>
